      "data": {
        "text": "**Considering External Providers**\n\nI'm currently evaluating external providers for upserting the JSON document, focusing on Cloud NoSQL databases. The frontrunners are AWS DynamoDB, Google Cloud Firestore, and Azure Cosmos. I need to weigh the pros and cons of each, considering factors like cost, scalability, and ease of integration with Python.\n\n\n**Selecting Firestore Provider**\n\nI've decided on Google Cloud Firestore as the external provider. It suits the requirements well and offers Python SDK support. The focus now is implementing the `upsert_document` function in `upsert_document.py`. This function will take the collection name, document ID, and data to handle upsert logic using the Firestore Python SDK. I'm prioritizing the provider-specific identifiers for the upsert functionality.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789867623554,
          "start": 1789867621767
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc6c7d87001sftSSgT8fYhcop",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc6c77a5001IMNDF6btvNVPi2",
      "session_id": "ses_f439388f8ffefRexoShdXzN1Ln",
      "time_created": 1789867621767,
      "time_updated": 1789867623555
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "31NUuoindSBF75xS",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import firestore\n\ndef upsert_document(collection_name: str, document_id: str, document_data: dict):\n    \"\"\"Upserts a JSON document into a Firestore collection by its primary identifier.\n\n    Args:\n        collection_name: The name of the Firestore collection.\n        document_id: The ID of the document to upsert.\n        document_data: The dictionary representing the JSON document to upsert.\n    \"\"\"\n    db = firestore.Client()\n    doc_ref = db.collection(collection_name).document(document_id)\n    doc_ref.set(document_data)\n    print(f\"Document {document_id} upserted in collection {collection_name}.\")\n\n",
            "filePath": "upsert_document.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
